      <script type="application/ld+json">{"@context": "http://schema.org", "@type": "MedicalWebPage", "about": {"@type": "WebPage", "alternateName": ["Influenza"], "name": "Flu"}, "author": {"@type": "Organization", "email": "nhswebsite.servicedesk@nhs.net", "logo": "https://assets.nhs.uk/nhsuk-cms/images/nhs-attribution.width-510.png", "name": "NHS website", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk"}, "breadcrumb": {"@context": "http://schema.org", "@type": "BreadcrumbList", "itemListElement": [{"@type": "ListItem", "item": {"@id": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/", "genre": [], "name": "Conditions A to Z"}, "position": 0}, {"@type": "ListItem", "item": {"@id": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/", "genre": ["Condition"], "name": "Flu"}, "position": 1}]}, "copyrightHolder": {"@type": "Organization", "name": "Crown Copyright"}, "dateModified": "2026-07-03T08:10:26+00:00", "description": "NHS information about flu, including symptoms, how to treat it yourself and when to get help.", "genre": ["Condition"], "hasPart": [{"@type": "HealthTopicContent", "description": "The symptoms of flu are similar to a very bad cold. They include a high temperature, an aching body, tiredness and a headache.", "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/SymptomsHealthAspect", "hasPart": [{"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "", "text": "<p>Flu symptoms come on very quickly and can include:</p><ul><li>a sudden high temperature</li><li>an aching body</li><li>feeling tired or exhausted</li><li>a dry cough</li><li>a sore throat</li><li>a headache</li><li>difficulty sleeping</li><li>loss of appetite</li><li>diarrhoea, tummy pain, feeling sick (nausea) and being sick (vomiting) \u2013 although these are less common in adults</li></ul><p>The symptoms are similar for children, but they can also get pain in their ear, sore eyes, <a href=\"/symptoms/swollen-glands/\">swollen glands</a> and appear less active.</p>"}], "headline": "Symptoms of flu", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/#symptoms"}, {"@type": "HealthTopicContent", "description": "Flu will usually get better in about a week if you rest, drink plenty of fluids and take painkillers.", "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/SelfCareHealthAspect", "hasPart": [{"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "", "text": "<p>If you have flu, there are some things you can do to help get better more quickly.</p>"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Do", "text": "<ul><li><p>rest and sleep</p></li><li><p>take <a href=\"/medicines/paracetamol-for-adults/\">paracetamol</a> or <a href=\"/medicines/ibuprofen-for-adults/\">ibuprofen</a> to lower your temperature and treat aches and pains</p></li><li><p>give <a href=\"/medicines/paracetamol-for-children/\">paracetamol</a> or <a href=\"/medicines/ibuprofen-for-children/\">ibuprofen</a> to your child if they're distressed or uncomfortable \u2013 check the packaging or leaflet to make sure the medicine is suitable for your child, or speak to a pharmacist or GP if you're not sure</p></li><li><p>drink plenty of water to avoid <a href=\"/conditions/dehydration/\">dehydration</a> (your pee should be light yellow or clear)</p></li></ul>"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Don't", "text": "<ul><li><p>do not give aspirin to children under the age of 16</p></li></ul>"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "A pharmacist can help with flu", "text": "<p>A pharmacist can give treatment advice and recommend flu remedies.</p><p>Do not take paracetamol and flu remedies that contain paracetamol at the same time as it's easy to take more than the recommended dose.</p>"}, {"potentialAction": {"@type": "ViewAction", "name": "Find a pharmacy", "target": "https://www.nhs.uk/service-search/pharmacy/find-a-pharmacy/"}}], "headline": "How to treat flu yourself", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/#self-care"}, {"@type": "HealthTopicContent", "description": "", "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/MedicalHelpUrgentHealthAspect", "hasPart": [{"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Ask for an urgent GP appointment or get help from NHS 111 if:", "identifier": "urgent", "text": "<p>\n You or your child have symptoms of flu and:\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n  you're worried about your baby's or child's symptoms\n </li>\n<li>\n  you're 65 or over\n </li>\n<li>\n  you're pregnant or have recently given birth\n </li>\n<li>\n  you have a long-term medical condition \u2013 for example, diabetes or a condition that affects your heart, lungs, liver, kidneys, brain or nerves\n </li>\n<li>\n  you have a weakened immune system \u2013 for example, because of chemotherapy or HIV\n </li>\n<li>\n  you feel very unwell\n </li>\n<li>\n  you feel short of breath\n </li>\n<li>\n  your symptoms do not improve after 7 days\n </li>\n</ul>\n<p>\n You can call 111 or\n <a href=\"https://111.nhs.uk/triage/check-your-symptoms\">\n  get help from 111 online\n </a>\n .\n</p>\n"}], "headline": "", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/#urgent-medical-help-old"}, {"@type": "HealthTopicContent", "description": "", "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/MedicalHelpEmergencyHealthAspect", "hasPart": [{"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Call 999 or go to A&E if:", "identifier": "immediate", "text": "<ul>\n<li>\n  you get sudden chest pain\n </li>\n<li>\n  you have severe difficulty breathing \u2013 you're gasping, choking or not able to get words out\n </li>\n<li>\n  you start coughing up blood\n </li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"block-action_link\">\n<a class=\"nhsuk-action-link\" href=\"https://www.nhs.uk/service-search/find-an-accident-and-emergency-service/\">\n<svg aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"nhsuk-icon nhsuk-icon--arrow-right-circle\" focusable=\"false\" height=\"16\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" width=\"16\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\">\n<path d=\"M12 2a10 10 0 0 0-10 9h11.7l-4-4a1 1 0 0 1 1.5-1.4l5.6 5.7a1 1 0 0 1 0 1.4l-5.6 5.7a1 1 0 0 1-1.5 0 1 1 0 0 1 0-1.4l4-4H2A10 10 0 1 0 12 2z\">\n</path>\n</svg>\n<span class=\"nhsuk-action-link__text\">\n   Find your nearest A&amp;E\n  </span>\n</a>\n</div>"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "A&E safety messaging", "text": "<p>Do not drive to A&amp;E. Ask someone to drive you or call 999 and ask for an ambulance.</p><p>Bring any medicines you take with you.</p>"}], "headline": "", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/#emergency-medical-help-old"}, {"@type": "HealthTopicContent", "description": "To reduce the spread of flu, wash your hands often, cover your mouth and nose when you cough or sneeze and bin used tissues straight away.", "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/ContagiousnessHealthAspect", "hasPart": [{"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "", "text": "<p>Flu is very infectious and easily spreads to other people. You're more likely to give it to others in the first 5 days after getting infected.</p><p>Flu is spread by germs from coughs and sneezes, which can live on hands and surfaces for 24 hours.</p><p>To reduce the risk of spreading flu:</p><ul><li>wash your hands often with warm water and soap</li><li>cover your mouth and nose with a tissue when you cough or sneeze (if you do not have a tissue, cough or sneeze into the bend of your elbow, not into your hand)</li><li>bin used tissues as quickly as possible</li></ul><p>Try to stay at home and avoid contact with other people if you have a high temperature, feel hot, cold or shivery, or do not feel well enough to do your normal activities.</p>"}], "headline": "How to avoid spreading the flu", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/#transmission"}, {"@type": "HealthTopicContent", "description": "You can help avoid flu by getting a flu vaccine every year.", "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/PreventionHealthAspect", "hasPart": [{"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "", "text": "<p>The flu vaccine helps protect against flu. It's safe and effective.</p><p>It's offered on the NHS every year in autumn or early winter to some adults and children at higher risk of getting seriously ill from flu.</p>"}], "headline": "Flu vaccine", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/#prevention"}, {"@type": "HealthTopicContent", "description": "Flu is a common infection that can easily spread to other people. It usually gets better on its own, but it can make some people seriously ill.", "hasHealthAspect": "http://schema.org/OverviewHealthAspect", "hasPart": [{"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Flu", "text": "Symptoms"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Flu", "text": "Self-care"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Flu", "text": "Transmission"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "headline": "Flu", "text": "Prevention"}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "text": "<p>The symptoms of flu are similar to a very bad cold. They include a high temperature, an aching body, tiredness and a headache.</p> "}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "text": "<p>Flu will usually get better in about a week if you rest, drink plenty of fluids and take painkillers.</p> "}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "text": "<p>To reduce the spread of flu, wash your hands often, cover your mouth and nose when you cough or sneeze and bin used tissues straight away.</p> "}, {"@type": "WebPageElement", "text": "<p>You can help avoid flu by getting a flu vaccine every year.</p> "}], "headline": "", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/#overview"}], "keywords": "", "lastReviewed": ["2026-02-03T15:00:00+00:00", "2029-02-03T15:00:00+00:00"], "license": "https://developer.api.nhs.uk/terms", "name": "Flu", "relatedLink": [{"@type": "LinkRole", "linkRelationship": "Navigation", "name": "Flu", "position": 0, "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/"}], "schemaVersion": "http://schema.org/version/13.0/", "url": "https://www.nhs.uk/conditions/flu/"}</script>





